# icons/actors.rec: which sprite-sheet tile draws each actors icon ID, one record each: heroes (class.<class>_male/_female), monsters (monster.<id>), uniques (unique.<name>), townspeople (npc.<name>) and corpses (corpse.<name>).
# Every other file names icons by these IDs, never by number; an ID the game asks for that no record defines
# stops the game at start with its name.
# Fields:
#   internal_name     the icon ID, "kind.snake_case_name"
#   icon              the tile's number on the mod's sprite sheet (classic_roguelike.png), row by row from 0
#   name              a description for the mod author; not read
#   reference_image   the original graphic it stands in for; not read
#
# Heaven&Hell's actor icons: sprite-sheet tiles by icon ID, the same convention every mod uses.
# The monster entries are seeded from the icon numbers the monsters themselves carried before the
# schema moved icons out of the content record.

